Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix: end quietly when the reader closes the pipe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`brit … | head` printed `Error: Broken pipe (os error 32)` and exited 1 for every
command, because Rust ignores SIGPIPE and the write error travelled up as a failure.
A broken pipe now ends brit without a message and with status 141, the status a shell
reports for Git killed by SIGPIPE, so `set -o pipefail` still sees it. Only the final
reporting in `brit-cli/src/main.rs` changes: a mutation still sees the write error
where it happens, rather than being killed mid-operation by a restored SIGPIPE.

Kept as its own commit so it can be dropped if another lane fixes the same line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
